/-!
# Morphisms out of an ideal-power multiple, restricted to the complement of the ideal

Let `X` be an algebraic space over a scheme `S` contained in a big fppf site `B`, let
`ℐ ⊆ 𝒪_X` be a sheaf of ideals, let `Z = V(ℐ)` be the closed subspace it cuts out and let
`U = X \ Z`.  [Stacks, Tag 07UM] asserts that, for `X` Noetherian, `G` coherent and `F`
quasi-coherent, restriction to `U` is a bijection

`colim_n Hom_{𝒪_X}(ℐⁿ G, F) ⟶ Hom_{𝒪_U}(G|_U, F|_U)`.

This file builds that map, proves the geometric input which makes it exist — over `U` the
inclusion `ℐⁿ G ⟶ G` *is* an isomorphism, because `ℐ` is the whole structure sheaf on every
étale chart of `X` all of whose points lie off `Z` — and proves that it is **injective when `F`
too is coherent**; for `F` merely quasi-coherent, which is what the tag asks, injectivity is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.canonicalMapToHomRestrict_injective` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/CoherentHomColimitInjective.lean`.  The
complement is referred to through the
point set `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealUnitLocus` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/IdealZeroLocus.lean`, so that no construction of the
closed subspace `V(ℐ)` is needed; for a closed subspace `Z` given in advance the point set of
its open complement *is* that unit locus, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.range_pointsMap_openComplement_subset_idealUnitLocus` below.

Everything is stated for an arbitrary étale morphism `j : Y ⟶ X` of algebraic spaces whose image
misses `Z`, not only for the inclusion of the open complement: the restriction functor used is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.etaleModulePullback`, plain reindexing of sections along
postcomposition of charts, and no argument below asks `j` to be an immersion.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.unitIdealSieve`: the sieve on an étale chart generated by the charts
  over it on which the sheaf of ideals is the whole structure sheaf.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowHomRestrict`: **the canonical map of the first display of
  [Stacks, Tag 07UM], term by term** — the restriction along `j` of a morphism `ℐⁿ G ⟶ F`, read
  as a morphism `G|_Y ⟶ F|_Y` through the isomorphism `ℐⁿ G|_Y ≅ G|_Y`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.homKernelSubmodule`: the sectionwise kernel of a morphism of
  `𝒪_X`-modules, as a submodule of the source; its membership condition is local because the
  target is a sheaf.  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.homKernelSubmoduleIso` identifies it with the
  categorical kernel.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.unitIdealSieve_mem_topology`: the charts carrying the unit ideal
  cover every chart all of whose points lie in the unit locus.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealSheaf_obj_eq_top_of_range_subset_idealUnitLocus`: **a sheaf of
  ideals is the whole structure sheaf on a chart all of whose points lie in its unit locus.**
  Membership in a sheaf of ideals is local, so this follows from that covering.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowSubmodule_obj_eq_top_of_range_subset_idealUnitLocus`: on such
  a chart the ideal-power multiple `ℐⁿ G` has all the sections of `G`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isIso_etaleModulePullback_idealPowModuleι`: **over an étale morphism
  whose image lies in the unit locus the inclusion `ℐⁿ G ⟶ G` becomes an isomorphism.**  This is
  the identification under which the first display of [Stacks, Tag 07UM] reads a morphism out of
  `ℐⁿ G` as a morphism out of `G|_U`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.range_pointsMap_openComplement_subset_idealUnitLocus`: the open
  complement of a closed subspace lands in the unit locus of its defining ideal sheaf, so the
  statements above apply to it.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowModuleι_comp_idealPowHomRestrict` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowHomRestrict_homOfLE`: the canonical map is restriction along
  `j`, and it agrees along the transition maps `ℐᵏ G ⟶ ℐⁿ G` of the direct system — which is
  what makes the family of maps a single map out of the colimit.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_idealPowModuleHomOfLE_comp_eq_zero`: **injectivity of the
  canonical map of the first display of [Stacks, Tag 07UM], for a coherent target.**  On a
  Noetherian algebraic space, a morphism `φ : ℐⁿ G ⟶ F` of coherent modules which vanishes on the
  sections over every chart carrying the unit ideal of `ℐ` — the chartwise reading of the
  vanishing of `φ|_U` — is already killed by the transition map `ℐᵏ⁺ⁿ G ⟶ ℐⁿ G` for some `k`.
  Coherence of `F` is more than the tag asks of it, so this statement does not carry the tag; see
  the note on its declaration.

## Implementation notes

The covering in `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.unitIdealSieve_mem_topology` is the family of charts
supplied, one for each point of the chart, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_idealUnitLocus_iff_exists_over`.  Its index type is the set of
points of the chart and so is not bounded by the universe of the schemes; this is why
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.ofArrows_mem_topology`, which takes no size bound on the
index type because membership in the small étale precoverage only depends on the presieve the
family generates in schemes, is used rather than
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale.IsCovering` directly.  Joint surjectivity of the family on
the points of the underlying *scheme* of the chart is read off the identification
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pointsToScheme` of the points of a represented presheaf with the points
of the representing scheme.

That the inclusion becomes an isomorphism is checked on sections: over a chart of `Y` the
restriction of `ℐⁿ G ⟶ G` along `j` is, on the nose, the inclusion of the sections of `ℐⁿ G`
over the composite chart of `X`, and those are all of the sections of `G` there.  Bijectivity on
sections is turned into invertibility through the abelian structure of
`CategoryTheory.PresheafOfModules`, which instance search does find — unlike the one on
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.Modules` — together with the fact that the forgetful functor from
sheaves of modules to presheaves of modules reflects isomorphisms.  The module universe is
pinned to the universe `u` of the schemes from that point on only because
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.Modules` is written at `Modules.{u, u}` by its consumers; the two
`obj = ⊤` statements above are at a free module universe.

## The injectivity argument

Injectivity needs no étale descent, and in particular none of the scheme case: it is the
argument of [Stacks, Tag 07UK].  Factor `φ : ℐⁿ G ⟶ F` as `ℐⁿ G ⟶ Q ⟶ F`, where `Q` is the
quotient of `ℐⁿ G` by the sectionwise kernel of `φ`.  That kernel is the categorical one, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.homKernelSubmoduleIso`, so `Q` is the cokernel of a map of coherent
modules and hence coherent; and over a chart carrying the unit ideal every section of `ℐⁿ G` is
killed by `φ`, so `Q` has no sections there and its support lies in `V(ℐ)`.  [Stacks, Tag 07UK]
then produces a `k` with `ℐᵏ Q = 0`.  Over a chart a section of `ℐᵏ⁺ⁿ G` becomes, on a covering
sieve, a sum of products of a `k`-fold product of sections of `ℐ` with a section of `ℐⁿ G` — that
covering is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_sieve_mem_pow_chartSectionIdeal_smul_top_of_mem_idealPowSubmodule`
— and each such product dies on the way to `Q`, so the composite into `Q` vanishes on that sieve
and hence vanishes.

Several steps are cut into their own private lemmas rather than inlined, because the kernel does
not typecheck the assembled proof within its step limit: in particular a `show` that unfolds the
composition of two morphisms of modules on sections is replaced by the `rfl` lemma
`modulesComp_val_app_apply`, stated at variable modules, and the transport along the equality of
two sections of `ℐⁿ G` is performed with `congrArg` rather than `rw`, so that no motive over these
types is ever built.

## What is not proved

**Surjectivity** of the canonical map is **not** proved here, and neither is the tag's "in
particular" display.  No hypothesis standing in for either is introduced: a hypothesis asserting
the conclusion over every chart would be the assertion itself.

Both are proved elsewhere in the tree, so nothing about [Stacks, Tag 07UM] is outstanding.
Surjectivity is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.canonicalMapToHomRestrict_surjective` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/CoherentHomColimitChartDescent.lean`, which runs the
source's argument — an affine surjective étale `W → X` with `W` and `R = W ×_X W` Noetherian
schemes, Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma [Stacks, Tag 01YB] over each, and descent — through the
chart transport of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/CoherentHomColimitChartTransport.lean`, with the exponent
of the ideal raised until the two relocalizations to the kernel pair agree.  The "in particular"
display is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.canonicalMapToSections_bijective`.  Both clauses and both
displays are assembled, at the tag's own hypotheses, in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/CoherentHomColimitBijective.lean`, which is where the tag's
covering set sits.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07UM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07UM)
